# GENERATED ARTIFACTS — never committed, and the reason is mechanical, not tidiness.
#
# `bank.sh` snapshots the working tree when it STARTS and refuses to commit if the tree
# changed while it ran (the sweep guard: it exists because a bank once swept another
# session's uncommitted work into an unrelated commit). Gate [3/4] REWRITES the retrieval
# index during that window — so a TRACKED index makes the guard fire on every bank that
# follows any content change, and only a second run succeeds. Measured in the 2026-08-27
# install dry-run. The guard is right; the tracked generated file was the defect.
rag/index.json

